{"id": "EUVD-2026-103721", "enisaUuid": "e31fabb5-18c4-3549-a711-2ee2ae6e87e8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: port100: reject frames whose declared length exceeds the received data\n\nport100_recv_response() passes the URB transfer buffer to\nport100_rx_frame_is_valid(), which checksums le16_to_cpu(frame->datalen)\nbytes of frame->data. datalen is a 16-bit field supplied by the device\nand is never checked against the number of bytes actually received\n(urb->actual_length), so a device reporting a datalen larger than the\nreceived frame makes port100_data_checksum() read out of bounds past the\ntransfer buffer.\n\nReject a response whose declared frame size does not fit the received\nlength before validating it.\n\nFound by 0sec (https://0sec.ai) using automated source analysis; the\nmissing bound is evident from source. Compile-tested.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d482995f0cdd0302450aa300c684c642d8ab31f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e8df087826b9999d1b83b06f5d85675d5a69c9e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db66a30588630c7de30ef033f00daddef69f6ad9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/144ad477c381e2c592b64898d04ab4ce03b32861", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4da1452e10c6472a4bac48dc2f6a35fff1fcd69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14b1467cfc6630583650f33538174c5a1ec685ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/035056e07ea65be670284246d9bc62f2f00ff4a3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/092c6a605cbd6414ef499834c2e0da69c2c3388e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98481", "GHSA-76wj-ccjf-8q4p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a1e45e1-8104-3525-8757-ea90d0a44267", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.13"}, {"id": "26f263bf-5d95-3817-a959-ec947fc52949", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": 